# Codex review (Resonance3D main-repo, XM.1 item 5): this submodule had no
# .gitattributes at all, so nothing normalised line endings on commit - a
# single tool writing one file in Windows text mode (Python's default
# open(..., 'w') translates \n to the OS-native line ending) silently
# converted a whole source file from LF to CRLF, which then merged as-is
# twice before being caught. The main Resonance3D repo already carries this
# exact rule for the same reason (see its own .gitattributes comment).
*.cpp text eol=lf
*.h   text eol=lf
